@* A broken rule, printed under the row that broke it.

   **Visible, never hover-only.** The rows already carry a term-description tip from the
   hover-description work, and a finding is tempting to fold into the same plumbing — but WCAG
   is explicit that information carried only by a tooltip is information some readers do not
   get, and a rule the character has broken is exactly that kind of information. This renders in
   the ordinary flow of the page. It is never the only place a finding is said, either — the GM
   review step still prints every one, in full, with the budget findings this component never
   sees.

   **A Warning can be dismissed; an Error cannot, and that is drawn here rather than trusted.**
   `IsError` gates the control below on the same field `Kind`/`Label` already read, so a caller
   handing this component an Error still gets no way to wave it away — `IsValid` on
   `ValidationResult` is "no Error", and a dismissable Error would let an illegal character read
   as legal on screen, against the settled rule that an illegal character is reported and never
   repaired. The findings this component is handed are already filtered to hide anything already
   dismissed — see `ChosenRow`, `AbilitiesTab` and `TalentsTab` — so what is drawn here is always
   what is currently on screen, dismissed or not.

   **The engine decides; this only prints what SheetFindings already routed.** Nothing here
   prices, validates, or decides which row an issue belongs to — that is SheetFindings' job,
   reading the SubjectKind/SubjectId/OwnerId CharacterValidator already filled in. This component
   receives a list already meant for it and draws it; dismissing one is a request to whoever fed
   it that list, never a decision this component makes about the character.

   **Error and warning are never colour alone.** A printed word leads every sentence, and the
   left edge differs in *style* as well as in colour — solid against dashed — because a colour
   difference alone fails WCAG 1.4.1 for the one reader in twelve who cannot use it. *@

@if (Issues is { Count: > 0 })
{
    <ul class="row-findings">
        @foreach (var issue in Issues)
        {
            <li class="finding @Kind(issue)">
                <span class="finding-kind">@Label(issue)</span>
                @issue.Message
                @if (!IsError(issue))
                {
                    <button type="button" class="btn small finding-dismiss"
                            aria-label="@($"Dismiss: {issue.Message}")"
                            @onclick="() => Dismiss(issue)">Dismiss</button>
                }
            </li>
        }
    </ul>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The findings that belong to this row, already routed by <see cref="SheetFindings"/> and
    /// already filtered to drop anything currently dismissed. Null or empty draws nothing — most
    /// rows break no rule, and a row that is fine should look exactly like one nobody has looked
    /// at yet.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<ValidationIssue>? Issues { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Raised when the reader dismisses one Warning. The feed point that supplied
    /// <see cref="Issues"/> owns the storage call and the redraw; this component only reports
    /// which issue was waved off.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<ValidationIssue> OnDismiss { get; set; }

    // Kept inside @code rather than written as `issue.Severity == ValidationSeverity.Error`
    // in the markup above: NoPageNamesATypeThisProjectDeclares strips the @code block before
    // it scans for a compound type name, and does not strip an ordinary C# statement sitting
    // inside a @foreach in the templated region — a type name written there prints on the
    // player's screen as far as that guard can tell.
    private static bool IsError(ValidationIssue issue) => issue.Severity == ValidationSeverity.Error;

    private static string Kind(ValidationIssue issue) => IsError(issue) ? "error" : "warning";

    private static string Label(ValidationIssue issue) => IsError(issue) ? "Error" : "Warning";

    private Task Dismiss(ValidationIssue issue) => OnDismiss.InvokeAsync(issue);
}
